# Enable Application Password / REST API authentication on LiteSpeed (Hostinger).
#
# WHY: By default this server strips the HTTP "Authorization" header before it
# reaches PHP, so WordPress never sees Application Password credentials and every
# authenticated REST request fails with {"code":"rest_not_logged_in"}.
#
# HOW: Add these lines to your site's .htaccess, INSIDE the "# BEGIN WordPress"
# block, right after the "RewriteEngine On" line. Then save.
#
#   RewriteEngine On
#   RewriteCond %{HTTP:Authorization} ^(.*)
#   RewriteRule .* - [E=HTTP_AUTHORIZATION:%1]
#   # --- end auth header pass-through ---
#
# If the RewriteRule form doesn't work on your setup, use this instead
# (either one is enough — don't add both):
#
#   SetEnvIf Authorization "(.*)" HTTP_AUTHORIZATION=$1
#
# After saving, clear LiteSpeed cache (LiteSpeed Cache -> Toolbox -> Purge All).
# Then Claude can authenticate and apply the SEO fixes via the REST API.
